   378	 1: for k = 0, 1, . . . , K do
   379	 2:   while xk is not optimal for ck do
   380	 3:      xk := aug(xk , ck )
   381	        k+1
   382	 4:   x     := xk
   383	 5: return xK+1 .
   384	     Here, aug(xk , ck ) stands for the solution returned by the augmentation
   385	oracle when called with input xk and ck . The condition of whether to continue
