Schulz explicitly assumes arbitrary integer costs and an explicitly known feasible solution, so the dossier’s attribution is accurate. Lemma A and the bit-scaling argument appear sound: every oracle target remains feasible, and coordinate flipping requires no closure of the instance family. I’m checking the rational-output arguments and the scope of the book-question claims next.
