   112	    Inverse problems under the ℓ∞ -norm have been studied in various settings. Xiaoguang [26]
   113	considered the inverse optimization problem of submodular functions on digraphs, and gave
   114	an LP-based algorithm that solves most inverse network optimization problems in polynomial
   115	time. Zhang and Liu [29] suggested a method for solving a general inverse LP problem including
   116	upper and lower bound constraints. In a later paper [19], the same authors studied the inverse
