   459	Sokkalingam [25] develops a duality theory for inverse linear problems under general “unorms”
   460	using duality results in convex analysis. A function k : Rn → R is called an unorm, if
   461	  1. k(x) ≥ 0 for all x ∈ Rn and k(x) = 0 if and only if x = 0,
   462	  2. k(λx) = λk(x) for λ > 0 and x ∈ Rn ,
   463	  3. k(x + y) ≤ k(x) + k(y) for x, y ∈ Rn .
   464	Its polar k 0 : Rn → R is defined by k 0 (x) := supy6=0 xt y/k(y).
